[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one parser fix queued. Its reports say
otherwise. Read by what the dates do, and by which tenant and form they came through, they hold
three problems. The queued fix covers only the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Closing #4471 when the parser fix ships leaves two live bugs with no ticket of their own.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/magiczna7/desk-4471/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/magiczna7/desk-4471/issues/2',
    'one-day-move': 'https://github.com/magiczna7/desk-4471/issues/3',
  }}
/>

## What each one is

- **`parser`** ([ticket](https://github.com/magiczna7/desk-4471/issues/1)): the shared parser
  reads every date month first; every tenant on file writes the day first. Day and month swap,
  through app, email and booking-v2 forms. This is what #4471 describes.
- **`hint`** ([ticket](https://github.com/magiczna7/desk-4471/issues/2)): booking-v3 prints
  `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what it says, and the form reads it the
  tenant's way. Same symptom, different code: the parser fix does not touch it.
- **`one-day-move`** ([ticket](https://github.com/magiczna7/desk-4471/issues/3)): no swap. The
  date moves by one day and the weekday with it, and one meeting showed on different days in two
  cities. That is time zones, not order. The desk already noted these reports
  (`desk-notes.json`); #4471 still counts them under `parser`.

## How they ended up in one ticket

Triage merges on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). All
three problems produce the same subjects ("Wrong date again", "Month and day swapped?"), so the
rule merged them without reading a body. Intake's tag does not help either: it guesses from the
reporter's browser, not the tenant, and splits the `hint` reports between both tags.

## For the desk

- Split by cause before marking a big ticket known. A date ticket needs the tenant's locale,
  its booking form and what the two dates in the body do to each other.
- Keep #4471 for `parser`. Move the other two to their tickets so they are not closed with it.

